@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Redgear X13 Pro: limited read-only research driver
+
+Device: owner-confirmed wired Redgear X13 Pro, VID:PID **1B80:B412**; USB product **MECHREV Gaming Mouse**, manufacturer **Jtech**. Native attribute revision **0x0713** is not a decoded firmware version. This identifier must not be extrapolated to all Redgear mice.
+
+On 2026-10-16, Windows HID descriptors reported interface 01 vendor collections FF00:0001 carrying feature reports 3/4/5/6, with full Windows buffer lengths 40/2049/6/8 bytes respectively. The driver accepts only a collection offering feature report 3 with 39 payload bytes. Keyboard/consumer/pointer and the other vendor collections are not status interfaces for this driver.
+
+The supplied hid.exe (SHA-256 ef665c1dd608656729c78d1cc003ad44ef50c15c7370e2a499f1b40fb87d808a) statically calls HidD_GetFeature for report 3, length 40, at VA 0x4058a4. Its wrapper at 0x402280 calls the HID API via the thunk at 0x51eb8e. No vendor executable was run. A separate native helper using only the documented GET_FEATURE operation read the exact connected mouse three times, approximately 100 ms apart, without any preliminary writes. All replies were identical:
+
+```text
+0305033100ff00000102030405060700ff000000ff000000ffffff0000ffffff00ffffffff000000
+```
+
+The fixture includes the report ID at byte 0. The 39-byte payload remains opaque: no DPI, polling, RGB, profile, firmware or checksum interpretation is claimed. These are direct native read samples of one state, not USBPcap captures or independent setting-change cases. Full raw evidence stays outside the upstream checkout, ignored locally; no proprietary binaries or user identifiers are redistributed.
+
+The codec checks only framing and returns a copy. Native framing includes the report ID (40 bytes); the separate WebHID/Bridge payload decoder requires 39 bytes without the ID. The driver opens the status device and calls receiveFeatureReport(3), retains a defensive copy of the reconstructed full report for local research, coalesces concurrent reads, enforces a two-second read timeout, and falls back to identity if reads fail. It suppresses further reads after failure until reconnect. It has **no setters, sendReport or sendFeatureReport path**. Settings remain disabled, required numeric telemetry uses hidden zero sentinels, active profile is unknown, and firmware is empty. `verified` remains false.
+
+Automated tests cover the physical fixture, wrong lengths/IDs, narrow identity/collection matching, nonzero DataView offsets, no writes, malformed/failed reads, timeout, and disconnect invalidation. The registry probe includes the measured collection shape. The local OpenMouse controller imports the client and includes it in NEEDS_OPEN.
+
+Owner confirmed successful connection through the browser picker in Edge; the visible title and heading were independently observed as "Redgear X13 Pro" with Connected/Wired status. Direct WebHID GET report 3 fails after 37 ms with "Failed to receive the feature report," and the app correctly falls back to identity only. This is an API failure before decoding, not evidence of malformed device bytes.
+
+With owner approval, official portable OpenMouse Bridge v1.0.0-beta.15 was run temporarily with isolated config, updates off and startup registration disabled. The archive matched its official SHA-256. Through Bridge the local app displayed the BRIDGE badge and successful read-only research notice. Three independent Bridge reads returned identical 39-byte payloads matching the native fixture after removal of its report-ID prefix. Bridge needs no system capture driver for this path. No vendor executable or HID write was performed. Cold physical reconnect, payload semantics and setting changes remain untested. `verified` remains false.
+
+Next: capture vendor startup and controlled before/after settings, establish payload semantics, add independent fixtures, then implement one proven setting at a time. Installing USBPcap, running original EXEs and the first write for each feature require owner approval. Firmware/bootloader/calibration writes are out of scope.
